{"id": "Q005", "card": {"answer_id": "560", "kb_version": 50, "as_of": null, "superseded_since": null, "client": null, "route": "lookup", "status": "answered", "rule": {"text": "The cut-off time for an invoice to be included in a payment run is 1 pm on the previous working day. [1] Payment runs are scheduled for Tuesday and Friday. [1]", "citations": [{"n": 1, "passage_id": "24ff09af33216f26bf19", "file": "PS-07_AP_SOP_v4.0_2026.docx", "short_label": "AP SOP v4.0 §9", "locator": "9", "section_title": "Payments", "doc_type": "sop", "status": "current", "quote": "Payment runs are on Tuesday and Friday. The cut-off for an invoice to be included is 1 pm on the previous working day."}]}, "working": null, "decision": "Cut-off is 1 pm on the previous working day", "exception_code": null, "next_owner": null, "older_sources": [{"topic": "Payment run schedule", "current_value": "1 pm", "older_value": "5 pm", "file": "PS-07_AP_SOP_v3.1_2023.docx", "locator": "AP SOP v3.1 §8", "superseded_by": "AP SOP v4.0 §9", "superseded_on": "2026-04-01"}, {"topic": "Payment run schedule", "current_value": "1 pm", "older_value": "5 pm", "file": "PS-07_desk_instructions_and_client_memos.docx", "locator": "Part F", "superseded_by": "AP SOP v4.0 §9", "superseded_on": "2026-04-01"}, {"topic": "Payment run schedule", "current_value": "Tuesday and Friday", "older_value": "Thursday", "file": "PS-07_AP_SOP_v3.1_2023.docx", "locator": "AP SOP v3.1 §8", "superseded_by": "AP SOP v4.0 §14", "superseded_on": "2026-04-01"}, {"topic": "Payment run schedule", "current_value": "Tuesday and Friday", "older_value": "Thursday", "file": "PS-07_desk_instructions_and_client_memos.docx", "locator": "Part F", "superseded_by": "AP SOP v4.0 §14", "superseded_on": "2026-04-01"}], "expert_tip": {"text": "Payment runs occur on Friday.", "author": "Lakshmi", "date": "2026-09-08", "citation": {"n": 0, "passage_id": "7c1d120ea568240a6e9a", "file": "PS-07_training_and_expert_transcripts.docx", "short_label": "Expert interview 1 [07:50]", "locator": "Expert interview 1 [07:50]", "section_title": "Lakshmi Reddy, Senior Processor", "doc_type": "interview", "status": "record", "quote": "Payment runs are Tuesday and Friday."}, "approved_by": null}, "route_to": null, "entities": [{"id": "9cb1508079ee39e919a9", "name": "invoice", "type": "invoice"}, {"id": "afea4ce79f8a48854046", "name": "payment run", "type": "paymentrun"}, {"id": "96979238aea4f4c3715f", "name": "Invoice retention period", "type": "topic"}], "related": ["What happens if an invoice misses the cut-off?", "Are there different cut-off times for MSME suppliers?", "How are payment runs scheduled around holidays?"], "latency_ms": 75902, "diagnostics": {"timings_s": {"route": 70.05, "retrieve": 4.4, "answer_and_check": 0.35, "attempts": 1}, "router": {"route": "lookup", "client": null, "confidence": 0.9, "out_of_scope_reason": "", "role": "ap_controller"}, "retrieval": {"scorer": "rerank", "top_score": 6.00184965133667, "passages": [["AP SOP v4.0 §9", "24ff09af33216f26bf19", 6.002], ["Video 1 [11:40]", "cbd8707434198f2a9f13", 1.724], ["Video 1 [06:55]", "fbbb4c331e748fe5fa18", -5.82], ["AP SOP v4.0 §12", "17c066174b5c8497f1c5", -6.297], ["Video 1 [04:30]", "732c3af92baad708588f", -6.691], ["Video 1 [02:10]", "72f14a5f302dcc6a4970", -6.764]], "facts": [337, 220, 531, 530, 529, 624, 535, 538, 532, 221]}, "verifier": {"verified": true, "problems": [], "attempts": []}}}}
{"id": "Q006", "card": {"answer_id": "561", "kb_version": 50, "as_of": null, "superseded_since": null, "client": null, "route": "lookup", "status": "answered", "rule": {"text": "A supplier whose aggregate annual turnover (AATO) in any financial year since 2017-18 has exceeded ₹5 crore must issue an e-invoice with an Invoice Reference Number (IRN) and QR code. [1] If such a supplier sends an invoice without an IRN, the invoice is not valid for input tax credit and is returned with the exception code IRN_MISSING. [1][2] The base value of an invoice missing an IRN must not be paid; a valid e-invoice will follow. [1]", "citations": [{"n": 1, "passage_id": "4e6e5c36ba75375f5adc", "file": "PS-07_AP_SOP_v4.0_2026.docx", "short_label": "AP SOP v4.0 §5.4", "locator": "5.4", "section_title": "E-invoices", "doc_type": "sop", "status": "current", "quote": "A supplier whose aggregate annual turnover (AATO) in any financial year since 2017-18 has exceeded ₹5 crore must issue an e-invoice with an Invoice Reference Number (IRN) and QR code."}, {"n": 2, "passage_id": "fa37880e315593668579", "file": "PS-07_AP_SOP_v4.0_2026.docx", "short_label": "AP SOP v4.0 §10", "locator": "10", "section_title": "Exceptions", "doc_type": "sop", "status": "current", "quote": "IRN_MISSING | E-invoice required but absent (5.4) | Supplier | Until e-invoice received"}]}, "working": null, "decision": "Above ₹5 crore aggregate annual turnover", "exception_code": null, "next_owner": null, "older_sources": [{"topic": "IRN requirement", "current_value": "₹5 crore", "older_value": "₹10 crore", "file": "PS-07_AP_SOP_v3.1_2023.docx", "locator": "AP SOP v3.1 §4", "superseded_by": "AP SOP v4.0 §5.4", "superseded_on": "2026-04-01"}, {"topic": "IRN requirement", "current_value": "₹5 crore", "older_value": "ten crore", "file": "PS-07_training_and_expert_transcripts.docx", "locator": "Video 2 [03:40]", "superseded_by": "AP SOP v4.0 §5.4", "superseded_on": "2026-04-01"}, {"topic": "IRN requirement", "current_value": "₹5 crore", "older_value": "₹10 crore", "file": "PS-07_desk_instructions_and_client_memos.docx", "locator": "Part F", "superseded_by": "AP SOP v4.0 §5.4", "superseded_on": "2026-04-01"}, {"topic": "irn_requirement.threshold_turnover", "current_value": "₹5 crore", "older_value": "1 October 2022", "file": "PS-07_training_and_expert_transcripts.docx", "locator": "Video 2 [03:40]", "superseded_by": "AP SOP v4.0 §5.4", "superseded_on": "2026-04-01", "reason": "Video 2 [03:40], dated 01 Nov 2022 is stale; AP SOP v4.0 5.4, dated 01 Apr 2026 is current."}], "expert_tip": null, "route_to": null, "entities": [{"id": "9cb1508079ee39e919a9", "name": "invoice", "type": "invoice"}, {"id": "6f9532bf9dfd91fa5e72", "name": "IRN", "type": "irn"}, {"id": "9419d012eda6da349252", "name": "supplier", "type": "supplier"}, {"id": "f1344187a241bc2e9d81", "name": "E-invoice", "type": "irn"}, {"id": "7b06e27e7932ae9f095d", "name": "e-invoice limit", "type": "irn"}], "related": ["What happens if a supplier below ₹5 crore turnover voluntarily issues an e-invoice with IRN?", "How is the AATO band determined and recorded for a supplier?", "What is the process for resolving an IRN_MISSING exception once the e-invoice is received?"], "latency_ms": 23625, "diagnostics": {"timings_s": {"route": 18.52, "retrieve": 3.63, "answer_and_check": 0.35, "attempts": 1}, "router": {"route": "lookup", "client": null, "confidence": 0.95, "out_of_scope_reason": "", "role": "tax_desk"}, "retrieval": {"scorer": "rerank", "top_score": 7.09132719039917, "passages": [["AP SOP v4.0 §5.4", "4e6e5c36ba75375f5adc", 7.091], ["AP SOP v4.0 §3.2", "a0c56e2c3d62e53aef37", -1.007], ["AP SOP v4.0 §10", "fa37880e315593668579", -2.995], ["DI-03 Part A, step 5", "022418586d5ee1f57041", -3.159], ["AP SOP v4.0 §8.1", "70416e5273b1509c18bb", -5.207], ["AP SOP v4.0 §5.1", "3db86dbc9e27ad62a645", -6.58]], "facts": [585, 418, 831, 589, 538, 537, 586, 72, 493, 587]}, "verifier": {"verified": true, "problems": [], "attempts": []}}}}
{"id": "Q007", "card": {"answer_id": "562", "kb_version": 50, "as_of": null, "superseded_since": null, "client": null, "route": "lookup", "status": "answered", "rule": {"text": "Input tax credit is claimed only for invoices that appear in the client's GSTR-2B. [1] GSTR-2B for a month is generated on the 14th of the following month. [1] If an invoice does not appear in GSTR-2B by the 14th, pay the base value on the due date and hold the GST amount until the invoice appears. [1] If the invoice is still missing after two further GSTR-2B cycles, raise NOT_IN_2B to the vendor relationship owner. [1]", "citations": [{"n": 1, "passage_id": "b69c0060ab5a623c596a", "file": "PS-07_AP_SOP_v4.0_2026.docx", "short_label": "AP SOP v4.0 §5.5", "locator": "5.5", "section_title": "GSTR-2B reconciliation", "doc_type": "sop", "status": "current", "quote": "Input tax credit is claimed only for invoices that appear in the client's GSTR-2B."}]}, "working": null, "decision": "GSTR-2B is the return used to decide ITC eligibility", "exception_code": null, "next_owner": null, "older_sources": [{"topic": "GST compliance checks", "current_value": "14th of the following month", "older_value": "20th of the following month", "file": "PS-07_AP_SOP_v3.1_2023.docx", "locator": "AP SOP v3.1 §4", "superseded_by": "AP SOP v4.0 §5.5", "superseded_on": "2026-04-01"}, {"topic": "GST compliance checks", "current_value": "14th of the following month", "older_value": "20th", "file": "PS-07_desk_instructions_and_client_memos.docx", "locator": "Part F", "superseded_by": "AP SOP v4.0 §5.5", "superseded_on": "2026-04-01"}, {"topic": "GST compliance checks", "current_value": "Pay the base value on the due date and hold the GST amount until the invoice appears in GSTR-2B.", "older_value": "hold GST portion", "file": "PS-07_AP_SOP_v3.1_2023.docx", "locator": "AP SOP v3.1 §4", "superseded_by": "AP SOP v4.0 §5.5", "superseded_on": "2026-04-01"}, {"topic": "gst_compliance.itc_claim_rule", "current_value": "Input tax credit is claimed only for invoices that appear in the client's GSTR-2B.", "older_value": "GSTR-2A", "file": "PS-07_AP_SOP_v3.1_2023.docx", "locator": "AP SOP v3.1 §4", "superseded_by": "AP SOP v4.0 §5.5", "superseded_on": "2026-04-01", "reason": "AP SOP v4.0 5.5, dated 01 Apr 2026 replaced AP SOP v3.1 4, dated 01 Jul 2023."}], "expert_tip": {"text": "Do not chase QRMP suppliers in month one or two of a quarter for missing invoices.", "author": "Imran", "date": "2026-09-15", "citation": {"n": 0, "passage_id": "fe8118ff141e89cbd526", "file": "PS-07_training_and_expert_transcripts.docx", "short_label": "Expert interview 2 [06:55]", "locator": "Expert interview 2 [06:55]", "section_title": "Imran Qureshi, Tax Desk Lead", "doc_type": "interview", "status": "record", "quote": "The SOP is right that we hold the GST — but chasing a QRMP supplier in month one or two of a quarter is pointless."}, "approved_by": null}, "route_to": null, "entities": [{"id": "4a29ab4f61c5265e5a12", "name": "GST", "type": "topic"}, {"id": "24d5298e0c608941f680", "name": "Input tax credit", "type": "gstin"}], "related": ["What happens if a supplier is a quarterly filer under QRMP?", "When should I raise NOT_IN_2B to the vendor relationship owner?", "What is the process for invoices missing IRN from e-invoice mandatory suppliers?"], "latency_ms": 228956, "diagnostics": {"timings_s": {"route": 108.29, "retrieve": 4.73, "answer_and_check": 114.49, "attempts": 1}, "router": {"route": "lookup", "client": null, "confidence": 0.95, "out_of_scope_reason": "", "role": "tax_desk"}, "retrieval": {"scorer": "rerank", "top_score": 0.9780833721160889, "passages": [["AP SOP v4.0 §5.5", "b69c0060ab5a623c596a", 0.978], ["AP SOP v4.0 §5.4", "4e6e5c36ba75375f5adc", -2.46], ["AP SOP v4.0 §2", "7ba624352fb111ab8f4c", -6.404], ["AP SOP v4.0 §5.3", "2e3ccb9ec585a5dee269", -6.527], ["Video 1 [08:20]", "46c1d777ed078bfe3738", -6.554], ["Expert interview 2 [06:55]", "fe8118ff141e89cbd526", -6.773]], "facts": [434, 590, 656